\\\", \\\"what does X mean?\\\", \\\"define X\\\", \\\"look up X\\\", or otherwise explicitly requests a concept definition from the repository's own content. DO NOT TRIGGER when: user is mid-writing-task (search-first handles pre-creation checks), asking about external tools or general knowledge, or using a word emphatically mid-sentence (content-conventions rule handles that).","path":"operations/engineering/fars/agentic/skills/concept-lookup/SKILL.md"},{"id":"context-budget","type":"skill","description":"Audits Claude Code context window consumption across agents, skills, MCP servers, and rules. Identifies bloat, redundant components, and produces prioritized token-savings recommendations.","path":"operations/engineering/fars/agentic/skills/context-budget/SKILL.md"},{"id":"decision-records","type":"skill","description":"Capture significant decisions made during sessions as structured records. Auto-detects decision moments, records context, alternatives considered, and rationale.","path":"operations/engineering/fars/agentic/skills/decision-records/SKILL.md"},{"id":"duty-dispatch","type":"skill","description":"Patterns for dispatching work to the right officer — matching tasks to offices, building proper prompts, choosing in-session vs external dispatch. Use when assigning work to agents.","path":"operations/engineering/fars/agentic/skills/duty-dispatch/SKILL.md"},{"id":"interpret-directives","type":"skill","description":"Interpret the captain's visionary musings into structured artifacts — ideas, plans, research tasks, term definitions. The captain produces inquiry; the first officer derives artifacts.","path":"operations/engineering/fars/agentic/skills/interpret-directives/SKILL.md"},{"id":"mcp-server-patterns","type":"skill","description":"Build and maintain MCP servers — tool registration, EAVT graph loading, stdio transport, .mcp.json config. Based on the 561-datastore server.","path":"operations/engineering/fars/agentic/skills/mcp-server-patterns/SKILL.md"},{"id":"rust-patterns","type":"skill","description":"Idiomatic Rust patterns, ownership, error handling, traits, concurrency, and best practices for building safe, performant applications.","path":"operations/engineering/fars/agentic/skills/rust-patterns/SKILL.md"},{"id":"rust-testing","type":"skill","description":"Rust testing patterns including unit tests, integration tests, async testing, property-based testing, mocking, and coverage.","path":"operations/engineering/fars/agentic/skills/rust-testing/SKILL.md"},{"id":"search-first","type":"skill","description":"Search for existing material before creating something new. Activates when starting new content, features, or infrastructure that might duplicate existing work.","path":"operations/engineering/fars/agentic/skills/search-first/SKILL.md"},{"id":"security-scan","type":"skill","description":"Proactive security scanning for code changes, hooks, tools, and infrastructure. Runs deterministic checks (secrets, injection, traversal) and escalates judgment calls to security-reviewer.","path":"operations/engineering/fars/agentic/skills/security-scan/SKILL.md"},{"id":"writing-botanical-terms","type":"skill","description":"How to write botanical term definitions — species, families, and foundational concepts. Covers the dual-file pattern (botanical science + gardening cultivation), taxonomy hierarchy, and quality standards for plant science content.","path":"operations/engineering/fars/agentic/skills/writing-botanical-terms/SKILL.md"},{"id":"writing-frontmatter","type":"skill","description":"Conventions for YAML frontmatter in this repository. Covers required fields, optional relations, and patterns by content type.","path":"operations/engineering/fars/agentic/skills/writing-frontmatter/SKILL.md"},{"id":"writing-gardening-texts","type":"skill","description":"How to write gardening texts — explanatory essays, analytical pieces, and diataxis-style explanations for the domesticity/gardening domain. Covers the distinct text types that emerged from encoding a growing guide into structured library content.","path":"operations/engineering/fars/agentic/skills/writing-gardening-texts/SKILL.md"},{"id":"writing-markdown","type":"skill","description":"Conventions for writing and editing any markdown file in this repository. Covers structure, linking, formatting, and style.","path":"operations/engineering/fars/agentic/skills/writing-markdown/SKILL.md"},{"id":"writing-operations-surveys","type":"skill","description":"How to write operations and work domain survey texts — cross-disciplinary methodology mapping, practice-grounded surveys that cover how work is planned, executed, tracked, and improved. Extends writing-surveys with operations-specific conventions. TRIGGER when: writing a survey in library/domains/humanities/domains/sociology/domains/work/ or surveying operational concepts (planning, scheduling, dispatch, tracking, review, feedback, governance). DO NOT TRIGGER when: the concept is purely philosophical (use writing-philosophy-surveys) or the survey is about conducting research (use research-survey).","path":"operations/engineering/fars/agentic/skills/writing-operations-surveys/SKILL.md"},{"id":"writing-philosophy-surveys","type":"skill","description":"How to write philosophical survey texts — tradition-mapping, deep source engagement, and the competing-accounts pattern. Extends writing-surveys with philosophy-specific conventions. TRIGGER when: writing a survey in library/domains/humanities/domains/philosophy/ or surveying a concept with deep philosophical roots (ontology, epistemology, ethics, action, identity, relation). DO NOT TRIGGER when: the concept is primarily practical/operational (use writing-operations-surveys) or purely technical.","path":"operations/engineering/fars/agentic/skills/writing-philosophy-surveys/SKILL.md"},{"id":"writing-surveys","type":"skill","description":"How to write a survey text — a grounded review of competing accounts, traditions, or methodologies on a concept. Covers structure, frontmatter, source standards, and the synthesis pattern. TRIGGER when: creating a new survey text, the user says 'write a survey', or a research-survey pass identifies a concept that needs a survey text. DO NOT TRIGGER when: conducting a survey (use research-survey), writing a regular text or term, or the user gives a specific file to edit.","path":"operations/engineering/fars/agentic/skills/writing-surveys/SKILL.md"},{"id":"writing-terms","type":"skill","description":"How to write a term definition file. Covers structure, voice, frontmatter, and patterns for simple, lesson-style, and formal terms.","path":"operations/engineering/fars/agentic/skills/writing-terms/SKILL.md"},{"id":"writing-texts","type":"skill","description":"How to write a text, paper, lesson, or essay. Covers structure, voice, frontmatter, and the writing process.","path":"operations/engineering/fars/agentic/skills/writing-texts/SKILL.md"}],"tfidf":[{"user":0.4261870230596063,"emphasizes":0.772760613339579,"word":0.5994738181995927,"check-term-definitions":0.772760613339579},{"modifying":0.772760613339579,"code":0.4981075411725515,"content":0.3248207460325652,"grep-before-edit":0.772760613339579},{"creating":0.28628307607575065,"overwriting":0.772760613339579,"file":0.4261870230596063,"read-before-write":0.772760613339579},{"look":0.15455212266791582,"repository":0.09962150823451031,"knows":0.07727606133395791,"concept":0.08523740461192127,"user":0.12785610691788188,"asks":0.09962150823451031,"trigger":0.08523740461192127,"mean":0.07727606133395791,"define":0.07727606133395791,"otherwise":0.07727606133395791,"explicitly":0.07727606133395791,"requests":0.07727606133395791,"definition":0.05994738181995927,"own":0.07727606133395791,"content":0.03248207460325652,"mid-writing-task":0.07727606133395791,"search-first":0.05994738181995927,"handles":0.15455212266791582,"pre-creation":0.07727606133395791,"checks":0.05994738181995927,"asking":0.07727606133395791,"external":0.0599473